# CivicConnect Unified Services Platform: Technical Specification for Unified Municipal Services Portal

**Document Version:** 1.0  
**Author:** Senior Technical Architect, Meridian Systems  
**Date:** [Current Date]  
**Project Phase:** Feature Expansion (Year 2)  
**Scope:** This specification finalizes the architecture for integrating all municipal services into a unified citizen portal. It includes the backend integration architecture, unified identity model, and citizen dashboard API. All designs align with the City of Meridian's approved data privacy policies (GDPR-inspired compliance) and existing infrastructure (AWS-based cloud with Kubernetes orchestration). Security features include OAuth 2.0 for authentication, JWT for session management, and role-based access control (RBAC) enforced at the API gateway level.

This specification assumes integration with existing legacy systems (e.g., utility billing via SAP, permit tracking via custom Oracle DB). No policy changes are proposed; all features build on approved requirements.

## 1. Backend Service Integration Architecture

The backend adopts a microservices architecture to enable modular integration of disparate municipal services. Services are containerized and deployed on Kubernetes, with an API gateway (e.g., Kong or AWS API Gateway) handling routing, rate limiting, and authentication. Event-driven communication uses Kafka for asynchronous updates (e.g., permit status changes triggering dashboard notifications).

### High-Level Architecture Diagram (Textual Representation)
```
[Citizen Portal Frontend (React.js)] 
  ↔ [API Gateway (OAuth/JWT Auth)]
    ├── [Unified Identity Service (UIS) - Handles citizen profiles]
    ├── [Dashboard Aggregator Service (DAS) - Aggregates data for personalized views]
    ├── [Utility Billing Service (UBS) - Integrates with SAP for payments/auto-pay]
    ├── [Permit Management Service (PMS) - Handles parking/building permits, status tracking]
    ├── [Library Management Service (LMS) - Card issuance/renewal]
    ├── [Recreation Booking Service (RBS) - Center bookings]
    ├── [Transit Pass Service (TPS) - Pass purchasing]
    └── [Event Bus (Kafka) - For cross-service notifications (e.g., deadline alerts)]
  ↔ [Data Layer: PostgreSQL (Primary DB) + Redis (Caching) + S3 (Document Storage)]
  ↔ [Legacy Integrations: SAP (Utilities), Oracle DB (Permits), External APIs (Transit/Recreation)]
```

### Integration Patterns
- **Synchronous API Calls:** Direct RESTful APIs for real-time operations (e.g., submitting a permit application).
- **Asynchronous Events:** Kafka topics for updates (e.g., `permit-status-updated` topic triggers dashboard refresh).
- **Data Synchronization:** ETL jobs (using Apache Airflow) run nightly to sync legacy data into the central PostgreSQL DB.
- **Error Handling and Resilience:** Circuit breakers (via Resilience4j) and retries for legacy system integrations. All services expose health endpoints for monitoring.
- **Scalability:** Auto-scaling pods based on CPU/memory thresholds. Caching in Redis for high-traffic endpoints (e.g., payment history).
- **Security:** All inter-service communication uses mutual TLS. Data encryption at rest (AES-256) and in transit (HTTPS).

Implementation Notes:
- Deploy as Helm charts for Kubernetes.
- Total estimated integration effort: 4-6 weeks, assuming legacy API wrappers are in place.

## 2. Unified Identity Model

The unified identity model centralizes citizen data in a single profile, stored in a PostgreSQL database schema named `citizen_identity`. This model aggregates service-specific data while maintaining data isolation for compliance (e.g., utility payment history is not accessible to library services without explicit consent).

### Data Model (JSON Schema Representation)
```json
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "title": "CitizenProfile",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "citizenId": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Unique UUID for the citizen account",
      "format": "uuid"
    },
    "personalInfo": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "fullName": { "type": "string" },
        "email": { "type": "string", "format": "email" },
        "phone": { "type": "string" },
        "address": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "street": { "type": "string" },
            "city": { "type": "string", "const": "Meridian" },
            "zipCode": { "type": "string" }
          },
          "required": ["street", "city", "zipCode"]
        }
      },
      "required": ["fullName", "email", "address"]
    },
    "serviceLinks": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "utilityAccountId": { "type": "string", "description": "Linked SAP account ID" },
        "parkingPermitId": { "type": "string" },
        "buildingPermitIds": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
        "libraryCardId": { "type": "string" },
        "recreationBookings": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
        "transitPassId": { "type": "string" }
      }
    },
    "preferences": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "autoPayEnabled": { "type": "boolean", "default": false },
        "notificationPreferences": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": { "type": "string", "enum": ["email", "sms", "app"] }
        }
      }
    },
    "usageHistory": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "serviceType": { "type": "string", "enum": ["utility", "permit", "library", "recreation", "transit"] },
          "eventType": { "type": "string", "enum": ["payment", "application", "booking", "renewal"] },
          "timestamp": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
          "details": { "type": "object" }  // Service-specific JSON blob
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["citizenId", "personalInfo", "serviceLinks"]
}
```

### Model Notes
- **Primary Key:** `citizenId` (UUID, auto-generated on registration).
- **Indexing:** Composite indexes on `email` and `address.zipCode` for quick lookups.
- **Data Lifecycle:** Profiles are soft-deleted after 7 years of inactivity per city policy. Auditing logs all changes via triggers.
- **Integration:** UIS microservice exposes CRUD operations for this model, with webhooks to notify other services on profile updates.

## 3. Citizen Dashboard API

The Citizen Dashboard API is exposed via the Dashboard Aggregator Service (DAS) as a RESTful API. It aggregates data from linked services to provide a personalized view, including upcoming deadlines

# Technical Specification: Wearable Integration for SafeFloor Industrial IoT Safety Platform

**Document Version:** 1.1 (Expansion from v1.0)  
**Author:** Senior Technical Architect, Meridian Systems  
**Date:** [Current Date]  
**Project Phase:** Module Expansion (9 months into 14-month engagement)  
**Client:** AmeriSteel Manufacturing  
**Overview:** This specification extends the AI safety monitoring platform to integrate wearable smart badges for individual worker safety. Wearables provide real-time location tracking via Ultra-Wideband (UWB) positioning, proximity alerts for heavy equipment and hazmat zones, biometric monitoring (heart rate and skin temperature) for heat stress detection, and cumulative noise exposure tracking against OSHA Permissible Exposure Limits (PEL, e.g., 90 dBA for 8 hours). Fatigue detection triggers on thresholds combining elevated heart rate and reduced movement variability, routing recommendations for mandatory rest breaks to shift supervisors.  

Integration builds on the existing hybrid cloud architecture (Azure IoT Hub with on-premises edge processing). Data privacy is maintained per client policy (e.g., anonymized worker IDs, consent-based tracking). Scalability supports 2,200 workers across 3 shifts, with peak wearable data rates of 1,000 updates/second. All components ensure low-latency alerts (<2 seconds for proximity warnings) and compliance with OSHA standards.

## 1. Data Models

Data models use JSON schemas, extending the existing sensor schemas for consistency. Timestamps are in ISO 8601 (UTC). Wearable data is stored in the time-series database (InfluxDB) with worker-anonymized identifiers.

### 1.1 Wearable Data Schema
Represents raw inputs from smart badges.

```json
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
